<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Ceramic Industries year shr, div flat.</title>
<headline>Ceramic Industries year shr, div flat.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended July 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     80.7	  vs 79.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 15.0	  vs same</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   14.49	 vs 14.23</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   21.71	 vs 15.00</p>
<p>    Tax			 7.29	  vs 0.77</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.03	  vs same</p>
<p>    Interest received     2.71	  vs 1.99</p>
<p>    Turnover		  134.46	vs 130.46</p>
<p>Disposal profit/loss  0.77 profit vs 1.01 loss</p>
<p>Div payable November 1</p>
<p>on register October 4</p>
<p>Full name: Ceramic Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Ceramic Industries, a maker of tiles to sanitaryware, said trading conditions had remained challenging with no real recovery in building activity or business confidence.</p>
<p>It added turnover had been suppressed by higher levels of imports in the pressed tile market and the disruption of commissioning a new plant at its Betta sanitaryware unit.</p>
<p>However, the firm predicted real growth in turnover and operating pofit in the current year due to the weakness of the rand creating stronger demand for local pressed tiles.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
